1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:06,293
Every day, India's food brands write off stock that sells too slowly.

2
00:00:07,443 --> 00:00:13,754
Too close to its date for quick commerce, it's destroyed, and its GST credit reversed.

3
00:00:15,404 --> 00:00:18,778
Smart-Clearance turns that write-off into recovery.

4
00:00:18,828 --> 00:00:26,184
Each brand gets its own workspace, where AI agents find the best exit for every pack at risk.

5
00:00:28,434 --> 00:00:39,121
Ten agents, built with Google's ADK, run on Cloud Run and think with Gemini. They walk every batch through nine stops, to one human yes.

6
00:00:40,871 --> 00:00:49,740
Meet Munchly Foods, our imaginary client: its distributors, kiranas, food banks and a marketplace.

7
00:00:49,790 --> 00:00:55,842
And the people you'll meet, as we follow two batches: one happy, one sad.

8
00:00:56,292 --> 00:01:05,057
In the console, Neha sets up a brand in minutes: its stock export, its people, its gates, its agents.

9
00:01:05,007 --> 00:01:08,894
Everyone signs in with Firebase, on their own device.

10
00:01:09,144 --> 00:01:16,409
The workspace installs as an app on any phone, tablet or laptop, so alerts reach everyone live.

11
00:01:17,059 --> 00:01:25,965
From the sell-through in BigQuery, the Watcher alerts Priya: Munchly's Mango Drink won't sell in its twenty-two days.

12
00:01:26,015 --> 00:01:33,424
Lakshmi Agencies photographs the label, and Vision, on Gemini Flash, matches it to the stock export.

13
00:01:33,474 --> 00:01:45,232
From the batch's sales history and Munchly's own rules, the Valuer prices each exit and the Router splits it. Priya approves with one tap.

14
00:01:45,282 --> 00:01:53,614
Outreach offers the packs to fifty-eight kiranas in their own language; each order lands on Priya's screen, live.

15
00:01:53,664 --> 00:02:00,712
Fifty-two shops take thirteen hundred and seventy-two packets, each with its own GST invoice.

16
00:02:00,762 --> 00:02:08,138
The godown's staff buy a hundred and fifty packs by UPI, and Vision checks the receipt against the count.

17
00:02:08,188 --> 00:02:13,400
Feeding India collects the last fifty-eight packs, and issues a donation receipt.

18
00:02:13,350 --> 00:02:19,391
Paperwork files every paper in Cloud Storage, and Lakshmi Agencies ends whole.

19
00:02:21,441 --> 00:02:29,571
But not every batch sells. Munchly's Masala Chips go to Rakesh Traders' kiranas in Nagpur, and just two order.

20
00:02:29,621 --> 00:02:39,456
On ExpireSoon, an imaginary near-expiry marketplace, the Negotiator counters a bid, and seven hundred and seventy-two packs sell.

21
00:02:39,506 --> 00:02:43,583
Five hundred and forty packets are left when the window closes.

22
00:02:44,033 --> 00:02:50,638
Rakesh's van delivers the two shops' orders, and the wholesaler's truck collects the lot.

23
00:02:50,688 --> 00:02:56,913
On expiry day, Rakesh must destroy them through an authorised agency, and prove it.

24
00:02:56,963 --> 00:03:05,218
At the landfill he photographs it, and the officer, two witnesses and Rakesh sign the certificate.

25
00:03:05,368 --> 00:03:12,137
Vision checks the photos; only on Priya's second yes are the certificate and credit note issued.

26
00:03:12,587 --> 00:03:22,379
Every step is on the record: an append-only audit trail in Cloud SQL, and requests traced end to end in Cloud Trace, with OpenTelemetry.

27
00:03:22,429 --> 00:03:31,913
Even here, Munchly recovers eleven thousand seven hundred rupees, fourteen thousand better than destroying it, and Rakesh ends whole.

28
00:03:31,963 --> 00:03:41,458
Impact posts every batch to its ledger in BigQuery: two point three tonnes kept from landfill this year, ready for BRSR.

29
00:03:41,508 --> 00:03:47,195
Next: WhatsApp, more Indian languages, and native iOS and Android apps.

30
00:03:47,145 --> 00:03:51,637
Try the guided demo at smartclearance-demo dot web dot app.

31
00:03:52,087 --> 00:03:57,960
Sign-ins for the live app on Google Cloud are in our deck; the sample data is on GitHub.
